    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d752">

                <pb facs="1229" n="1215" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg1215"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">340.1115A/11–844: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Harrison</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bern</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-11-08T11:00:00+01:00">November 8,
                            1944—11 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 8—9:50 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>7406. American Interests—Liberated Italy. Legation’s 5150, August 9, 9 p.m.
                    Foreign Office note November 2 states American representatives, according
                    telegram from Swiss Legation Rome, in <pb facs="1230" n="1216" xml:id="pg1216"/>
                    southern Italy have taken over completely from October 31, all matters
                    concerning American interests in Rome area. From that date Swiss Legation
                    discontinued payment relief.</p>
                <p>Protection American interests in Florence consular district not yet turned over
                    to American representatives. Accordingly Swiss Consulate that city will continue
                    these functions.<anchor n="87" xml:id="d752-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harrison</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d752-f1" n="87" xml:id="d752-f1-content">
                <p>Telegram 8210, December 18, from Bern, indicated that according to Swiss Foreign
                    Office note of December 16, “Swiss Consulate Florence continues protection of
                    American interests in provinces Florence, Arezzo, Livorno, Pisa, Ravenna,
                    Apuania, Forli, Lucas [<hi rendition="#italic">Lucca?</hi>], Pistoia, and Siena”
                    (125.7711/12–1844).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
